    "evidence_text": "This increased risk also applied to albumin 5%.\n\nPreoperative statin treatment reduces systemic inflammatory response and myocardial damage in cardiac surgery.\n\nRESULTS The baseline, operative and postoperative morbidity and mortality characteristics were similar for both the groups.\n\nThe impact of hydroxyethyl starches in cardiac surgery: a meta-analysis\n\nSimilar results were found for transfusion needs.\n\nFollow-up continued until the 10th postoperative day.   \n\n\nChildren who received dexamethasone received significantly less ibuprofen.\n\nThere were 26 postoperative bleeding episodes in 22 children.\n\nEight children had to undergo emergency reoperation because of bleeding, all of whom had received dexamethasone.\n\nThe trial was stopped early for safety reasons.   \n\n\nINTERVENTION Universal prestorage leukoreduction program introduced by 2 Canadian blood agencies.\n\nSecondary outcomes included rates of posttransfusion fever and antibiotic use.   \n\n\nDexamethasone decreases vomiting by children after tonsillectomy.\n\nAnesthesia was maintained with N2O and halothane.\n\n2 min, mean +/-\n\nSD (P < 0.001).\n\nRESULTS Eighteen trials with 970 total patients were included.\n\nAlbumin improved hemodynamics.",
